# doc-router — example environment file.
#
# Copy this to `.env` at the workspace root and fill in only the lines you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so never put a real key here.
#
# Who reads this file:
#   * `doc-router-bench` loads it at startup (workspace root only) and prints the
#     names — never the values — it loaded to stderr.
#   * The `doc-router` CLI and the Python bindings do NOT read it. They read the
#     real process environment, so `export`/`set -a` it yourself, or run them via
#     a tool that loads dotenv files.
#
# A variable already exported in your shell always wins over a line here.
# A missing file is not an error. A malformed line is skipped, not fatal.
# `export KEY=value` is accepted; one matching pair of surrounding quotes is
# stripped; everything after the first `=` is the value.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OCR provider — a LiteLLM proxy exposing POST <base>/v1/ocr
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Bearer token for the proxy. Read by `doc-router run` (as a fallback for
# `--api-key`) and by crates/doc-router-py/examples/litellm_adapter.py.
# LITELLM_API_KEY=

# Checked after LITELLM_API_KEY, in that order, by the same two callers.
# LITELLM_PROXY_API_KEY=

# Proxy origin, WITHOUT the /v1/ocr path. Read by the example adapter only —
# the Rust CLI takes it as the required `--base-url` flag instead.
# LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://0.0.0.0:4000


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jev judge — TypeSafe System One (crates/doc-router-jev)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setting one of these keys is the ONLY thing that turns the `jev` and
# `jev_gated` judges on. With neither set, doc-router-bench prints
# `skipped judge ...` and carries on with the heuristic baseline.

# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# Checked after TYPESAFE_API_KEY, in that order.
# JEV_API_KEY=

# Override the API origin. Default: https://api.typesafe.ai
# (the endpoint path /v1/systemone is appended and is not configurable).
# TYPESAFE_BASE_URL=

# Override the model id. Default: jev-latest
# TYPESAFE_MODEL=
